note Oracle layout of Allen's startup sound; composed after chirp.om by check.sh.
note Writes to fd 1 the exact file aienux native/kernel/ui/tests/chirp_test.c writes as chirp.wav
note (write_wav(path, s, N), N = CK_CHIRP_FRAMES = 590400): 2 channels, 16-bit, 48000 Hz, frames 0
note to 590400 (0 ms to 12300 ms of the night), left equal to right. check.sh compares it byte for
note byte with that C program's output, built from the pinned aienux source, so the Omega port is
note checked against the original, not against itself.

fn main to int
setup
put ofd 0 1
owav 2 FEND
f = ulong 0
note 590400 frames, one pass each.
while lt f FEND bound 590400
v = sample f
osample v
osample v
f = add f 1
end
oflush
ret 0
end
